Q1. Explain the order you placed your featured route and your detail route in, and what would happen if you swapped them.

I placed the featured route before the detail route because Laravel reads routes from top to bottom and uses the first route that matches the URL. If I swapped them, the {id} route would match the word featured as an ID, so the featured page would not load and it would return a 404 Not Found error.

Q2. What happens when someone visits an ID that does not exist in your data, and what did you write to make that happen?

If someone visits an ID that is not included in my movie data, Laravel displays a 404 Not Found page. I made this happen by checking if the movie ID exists, and if it does not, I used abort(404) in my MovieController.

Q3. Why do your links use route names instead of typed URLs? Give one concrete thing that would break if they did not.

I used route names instead of hardcoded URLs because they make the application easier to maintain. If I change a route's URL later, links that use route names will still work, while hardcoded URLs would break and would need to be updated everywhere in the project.
